#
# CTS buffer mixes (grep of <block>.phys_4.75.v):
#  anchor/commit/schedule: 33x buf_16 + 16x buf_8 (+0/0/6 inv loads) — IDENTICAL trunk
#    skeleton at 160-188 flops: small-N tree cost is a geometric floor, not per-flop.
#  icache: 33x buf_16 + 21x buf_8 + 180x buf_4 + 30 inv loads (1288 sinks -> 170 clusters)
#  execA: 129x buf_16 + 692x buf_8 + 1x buf_2 + 147 inv loads (3704 sinks -> 549 clusters)
#
# RESULT: E0_ff is FLAT (58.80-59.07 fJ over 160-3704 flops, spread 0.5%) — the flop
# clock-pin floor is genuinely per-flop linear. E_tree/flop is strongly SUBLINEAR in N:
# 44.3 fJ at N=188 -> 18.19 fJ at N=1288 (icache) / 29.75 fJ at N=3704 (execA). The
# assumed exactly-linear 44.334 fJ/flop OVERSTATES the chip tree term. The large-N spread
# (18.2 vs 29.8) tracks die area per flop (icache 98.9 um2/flop, execA 158.9): tree power
# = per-sink cap + trunk that grows with die area, not flop count alone.
#
# Scaling fits (least squares, see session derivation; small-N points sit on the trunk
# floor and no smooth law fits them — the floor amortizes away at chip scale):
#   P_clk = b*N + c*A  (anchored by the two large blocks, errors +3.6%/-0.2% there):
#     b = 2.05e-07 W/flop, c = 3.80e-08 W/um2 (=0.181 fJ/um2/cycle at 4.75 ns)
#     chip N=35004: E_tree/flop = 18.9 fJ (icache-like area/flop) .. 29.7 fJ (execA-like)
#   MEASURED BRACKET to replace the 44.334 assumption: E_tree(chip) in [18.2, 29.8]
#   fJ/flop/cycle, i.e. 0.41x-0.67x of the single-anchor linear extrapolation.
#   (b/c trade off with only 2 large-N points; prefer the bracket + area/flop
#   interpolation E_tree/flop ~= 18.19 + 0.193*(area_per_flop_um2 - 98.9) fJ, valid
#   98.9..158.9 um2/flop, over the raw b,c coefficients.)
#
